KNOWNBUG
s_eventually_assumption1.sv
--bound 2
^\[main\.a0\] always \(s_eventually \[2:3\] main\.c == 3\): ASSUMED$
^\[main\.p0\] always !main\.bad: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
property_obligations_rec (src/trans-word-level/property.cpp) truncates
the range of sva_ranged_s_eventually at the last time frame.  Here the
assumption can only be satisfied at the omitted frame, so the truncated
assumption becomes false and makes the trace set empty.  EBMC currently
reports the unrelated assertion as PROVED up to bound 2, although bad_in
can immediately refute it.  The same truncation causes the existing
s_eventually5 KNOWNBUG false-refutation case when the operator is an
assertion.  This test records the false-PROVED assumption manifestation.
